  "id": "DrugBank_DB14738 - MONDO_grouped_15787_15788",
  "verbalization": "Turoctocog Alfa Pegol is associated with Hemophilia, a condition characterized by impaired blood clotting, and it is indicated for treating Symptomatic Form Of Hemophilia In Female Carriers. This relationship is supported by the fact that Turoctocog Alfa Pegol is a recombinant coagulation factor, specifically designed to replace deficient clotting factors in patients with Hemophilia. The evidence suggests that Turoctocog Alfa Pegol is used to treat a form of Hemophilia that is particularly prevalent in female carriers, likely due to the unique genetic and physiological factors that affect coagulation in this population. The indirect pathway through Coagulation Factor Viia Recombinant Human or Coagulation Factor Ix Human further underscores the role of recombinant clotting factors in managing this condition. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of recombinant clotting factor therapy in treating Symptomatic Form Of Hemophilia In Female Carriers, particularly in cases where traditional treatments may be less effective.",
